  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have several stakeholders who want different things from the same piece of work. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what each of them is measured on$qb$, $qb$Ask each what they most need from it$qb$, $qb$Work out which of them has the final say$qb$, $qb$Find a version that partly satisfies everyone$qb$, $qb$Ask them to agree among themselves first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to do after resolving a customer's problem?$qb$, $qb$Find out what allowed the problem to happen$qb$, $qb$Check that the customer is satisfied with the outcome$qb$, $qb$Record what happened and how it was resolved$qb$, $qb$Tell the team so they can avoid the same thing$qb$, $qb$Move on, since the problem has been dealt with$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an optical laboratory that makes lenses for opticians. One optician has started returning about one order in ten as unsatisfactory. The lenses meet the specification he sends. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Visit and watch how the lenses are being fitted, then work back from there$qb$, $qb$Ask him what specifically is unsatisfactory about the returned lenses$qb$, $qb$Check your own process against the specifications he has sent$qb$, $qb$Ask him to be more precise in the specifications he sends$qb$, $qb$Replace the returns and treat it as a cost of the account$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a wedding hall. A family has booked for two hundred guests and now says four hundred are coming. The hall holds two hundred and fifty. The wedding is in six weeks. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell them today what the hall can hold and what the options are$qb$, $qb$Tell them the hall cannot take four hundred people$qb$, $qb$Ask them to reduce the guest list to two hundred and fifty$qb$, $qb$Look at whether the space could be extended for the day$qb$, $qb$Take the booking and manage the crowding on the day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a tuition centre for adults. Attendance in one course has dropped from twenty to eight over six weeks. Nobody has cancelled or complained. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Contact the twelve who stopped coming and ask what happened$qb$, $qb$Ask the eight still attending what has changed$qb$, $qb$Look at what changed in the course six weeks ago$qb$, $qb$Offer the twelve a discount to come back$qb$, $qb$Continue with the eight, since nobody has complained$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a mobile library that visits villages weekly. One village has had almost no borrowers for two months, though it used to be busy. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Go early one week and ask people in the village what changed$qb$, $qb$Ask the last few borrowers there why numbers have dropped$qb$, $qb$Check whether the stop time has changed recently$qb$, $qb$Change the stock you take to that village$qb$, $qb$Drop the stop and use the time on busier villages$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a tyre fitting bay. A fleet customer has complained that your work takes too long. Your fitting times are the same as everyone else's in the trade. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find out what the delay costs him and where his time actually goes$qb$, $qb$Ask him what he was expecting the job to take$qb$, $qb$Explain that your fitting times match the trade standard$qb$, $qb$Offer to fit his vehicles outside your busy hours$qb$, $qb$Offer him a discount to make up for the wait$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supply poultry to restaurants. One customer has asked for deliveries an hour earlier. Your round is already tight and moving him would delay two others. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask why the earlier time matters, since something else may solve it$qb$, $qb$Explain that moving him would delay two other customers$qb$, $qb$Ask the other two whether a later delivery would suit them$qb$, $qb$Move him earlier and absorb the delay to the others$qb$, $qb$Decline, since the round cannot be changed for one customer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a greeting card printing business. A retailer who has bought from you for eight years has not ordered this season. He has not said anything. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Call him and ask what has changed$qb$, $qb$Call him to check whether the order was missed$qb$, $qb$Send him the new season's samples again$qb$, $qb$Offer him a better price to prompt an order$qb$, $qb$Wait, since he may order later in the season$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a sports equipment shop. A school has asked for a quote for forty hockey sticks. You could supply cheaper sticks that would suit beginners better. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask who will be using them, then quote for what suits$qb$, $qb$Quote for both and explain the difference between them$qb$, $qb$Price what they asked for and mention the alternative$qb$, $qb$Send the quote exactly as requested, since that is what was asked$qb$, $qb$Substitute the cheaper sticks without saying you have changed anything$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a community centre. A group that has hired your hall every Tuesday for years has been given a worse room since your refurbishment. They have not complained. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Speak to them about the change and sort out the room$qb$, $qb$Move them back to a room like the one they had$qb$, $qb$Ask them whether the new room is working for them$qb$, $qb$Explain that room allocation changed with the refurbishment$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since they have not raised any objection$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a guest house. A regular guest has asked for a room on the ground floor. Your ground floor rooms are your most expensive. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask why the ground floor matters before talking about price$qb$, $qb$Offer the ground floor room at the higher price$qb$, $qb$Explain that ground floor rooms cost more$qb$, $qb$Give him the ground floor room at his usual rate$qb$, $qb$Offer him the lift as an alternative to moving rooms$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You service water purifiers. A customer has called out three times in two months for the same fault. Each visit fixed it temporarily. How do you handle the fourth call?$qb$, $qb$Look for what keeps causing it rather than fixing it again$qb$, $qb$Replace the part that keeps failing$qb$, $qb$Ask the customer what happens just before it fails$qb$, $qb$Fix it again and monitor how long it lasts$qb$, $qb$Suggest the customer replaces the whole unit$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manufacture uniforms. A hotel has ordered the same uniform for four years. Staff there have started altering them, which suggests the fit is wrong. Nobody has told you. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask the hotel what staff are changing and why$qb$, $qb$Ask the hotel whether there is a problem with the fit$qb$, $qb$Offer to review the sizing on the next order$qb$, $qb$Mention it to the hotel manager next time you visit$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the hotel keeps reordering$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a boat hire business. A customer has booked for a Saturday when the forecast is poor. He has travelled a long way and does not want to cancel. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell him plainly what the conditions will be like, then let him decide$qb$, $qb$Advise him to rebook for a better day$qb$, $qb$Offer him a free rebooking if he cancels now$qb$, $qb$Let him go out, since he has decided he wants to$qb$, $qb$Cancel the booking on safety grounds$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CSF-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A5-03$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a spice mill. A wholesaler has asked for a finer grind than you normally produce. Changing the setting would slow your line for everyone. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what the finer grind is needed for before changing anything$qb$, $qb$Work out what the slower line would cost you$qb$, $qb$Offer to run his order as a separate batch$qb$, $qb$Tell him the grind cannot be changed$qb$, $qb$Change the setting and absorb the slower line$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-001$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Work handed over with the decisions kept back is not delegation but ______.$qb$, $qb$instruction$qb$, $qb$training$qb$, $qb$sharing$qb$, $qb$planning$qb$, $qb$reporting$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-002$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Telling someone what result you need leaves them free to choose the ______.$qb$, $qb$method$qb$, $qb$deadline$qb$, $qb$budget$qb$, $qb$helper$qb$, $qb$standard$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-003$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A manager who checks every step teaches the team to wait for ______.$qb$, $qb$permission$qb$, $qb$freedom$qb$, $qb$deadlines$qb$, $qb$payment$qb$, $qb$praise$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-005$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone doing a task for the first time needs to know what ______ looks like.$qb$, $qb$finished$qb$, $qb$hard$qb$, $qb$quick$qb$, $qb$expensive$qb$, $qb$routine$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Taking a job back the moment it goes wrong removes the chance to ______.$qb$, $qb$learn$qb$, $qb$finish$qb$, $qb$explain$qb$, $qb$report$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A person given responsibility without authority will have to ______ for everything.$qb$, $qb$ask$qb$, $qb$wait$qb$, $qb$pay$qb$, $qb$apologise$qb$, $qb$account$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking for an update whenever you feel like it usually tells the person more about your ______ than about the work.$qb$, $qb$worry$qb$, $qb$seniority$qb$, $qb$schedule$qb$, $qb$standards$qb$, $qb$preferences$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Delegation fails most often not from poor ability but from unclear ______.$qb$, $qb$expectations$qb$, $qb$methods$qb$, $qb$training$qb$, $qb$supervision$qb$, $qb$resources$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who is never given difficult work never becomes ready for ______.$qb$, $qb$it$qb$, $qb$training$qb$, $qb$praise$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$recording$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking how someone plans to do it is more useful than telling them how you yorself ______.$qb$, $qb$would$qb$, $qb$pay$qb$, $qb$should$qb$, $qb$must$qb$, $qb$can$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Handing a task over at the last minute leaves the other person no time to ______ it.$qb$, $qb$improve$qb$, $qb$accept$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$price$qb$, $qb$repeat$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Giving someone a small job first tells you how they work before the ______ is high.$qb$, $qb$risk$qb$, $qb$pay$qb$, $qb$workload$qb$, $qb$deadline$qb$, $qb$standard$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$If you cannot say what good closure would look like, the task is not ready to be ______.$qb$, $qb$given$qb$, $qb$started$qb$, $qb$priced$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$filed$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A manager who is the only one who can do something has built a ______, not a skill.$qb$, $qb$risk$qb$, $qb$career$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$reputation$qb$, $qb$shortcut$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are handing a task to someone who has not done it before. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$That she knows what the finished result should look like$qb$, $qb$That she knows each step in the right order$qb$, $qb$That she knows who to ask if she is stuck$qb$, $qb$That she knows when it has to be finished$qb$, $qb$That she knows why the task matters$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have delegated a job and the person is doing it differently from how you would. The result will be fine. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Let her carry on with her own method$qb$, $qb$Ask her why she has chosen that method$qb$, $qb$Mention how you would have approached it$qb$, $qb$Ask her to use the method you would use$qb$, $qb$Watch closely in case the result is not fine$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably stops a delegated task coming back to you half done?$qb$, $qb$Agreeing what finished means before it starts$qb$, $qb$Setting a clear deadline for it$qb$, $qb$Checking on progress partway through$qb$, $qb$Choosing the right person for it$qb$, $qb$Explaining the task thoroughly$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You delegated something and it has gone wrong. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what was unclear when you handed it over$qb$, $qb$Find out what she did differently from what you expected$qb$, $qb$Fix the problem and hand it over again$qb$, $qb$Take the task back and do it yourself$qb$, $qb$Ask her to put it right and check it afterwards$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member has asked to take on something you usually do yourself. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Give her the whole task with the decisions that go with it$qb$, $qb$Give her the task and stay available for questions$qb$, $qb$Give her part of it and see how she manages$qb$, $qb$Explain how you do it and let her copy that$qb$, $qb$Keep it, since you can do it faster yourself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are too busy and need to hand something over. What should you hand over first?$qb$, $qb$Something with a clear result that someone else could own$qb$, $qb$The task that takes you the most time$qb$, $qb$The task you find least interesting$qb$, $qb$The task that is easiest to explain$qb$, $qb$The task with the least risk attached$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when someone is given a task but not the authority to make decisions on it?$qb$, $qb$They come back to you for each decision$qb$, $qb$They make decisions they should not make$qb$, $qb$They take longer than the task needs$qb$, $qb$They avoid the difficult parts$qb$, $qb$They do only what they were told$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have delegated work and want to know how it is going. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Agree at the start when you will both review it$qb$, $qb$Ask her for an update when you want one$qb$, $qb$Ask her to tell you if anything goes wrong$qb$, $qb$Check the work as it is produced$qb$, $qb$Wait until it is finished and see$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A person you delegated to has come back with a question you think she could answer herself. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what she thinks and back her judgement$qb$, $qb$Answer it and mention she could have decided$qb$, $qb$Answer it, since she has already asked$qb$, $qb$Tell her to make the decision herself$qb$, $qb$Ask her why she is unsure about it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are handing a task to a colleague and need it done to a standard you find hard to describe. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Show them an example of the standard you mean$qb$, $qb$Explain the standard as carefully as you can$qb$, $qb$Ask them to check with you before finishing$qb$, $qb$Do the first one together and hand over the rest$qb$, $qb$Do it yourself, since the standard is hard to explain$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A task you delegated is late and the person has not told you. What is most useful to establish?$qb$, $qb$Whether she knew it was late$qb$, $qb$Why the task has taken longer$qb$, $qb$Whether she needed help she did not ask for$qb$, $qb$When it will now be finished$qb$, $qb$Why she did not tell you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have two people who could take on a task. One is faster, one would learn more from it. What matters most in choosing?$qb$, $qb$How much time there is before it is needed$qb$, $qb$Whether the work could be put right if it went wrong$qb$, $qb$Which of them wants it more$qb$, $qb$How busy each of them is this week$qb$, $qb$Who has done something similar before$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone has done a delegated task well but differently from your instructions. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what led her to change it$qb$, $qb$Accept the result and say nothing$qb$, $qb$Point out that she departed from the instructions$qb$, $qb$Praise the result and repeat the instructions for next time$qb$, $qb$Ask her to follow the instructions in future$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to say when handing over a task you care about?$qb$, $qb$What you want the result to achieve$qb$, $qb$How you would do it yourself$qb$, $qb$What has gone wrong with it before$qb$, $qb$How important the task is$qb$, $qb$That you are available if needed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are away for a week and someone is covering your work. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$That she can decide the things that will come up$qb$, $qb$That she knows what tasks need doing$qb$, $qb$That she can reach you if necessary$qb$, $qb$That she knows who to ask for help$qb$, $qb$That everything is written down for her$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member consistently returns delegated work needing changes. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Look at what you are giving her, not only what she returns$qb$, $qb$Explain more clearly what you want next time$qb$, $qb$Ask her what she finds unclear about the task$qb$, $qb$Check the work earlier so changes cost less$qb$, $qb$Give the work to someone else instead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have delegated something and find yourself thinking about it constantly. What does this suggest?$qb$, $qb$You handed over the task but not the responsibility$qb$, $qb$You do not trust the person you gave it to$qb$, $qb$The task matters more than you admitted$qb$, $qb$You should check on how it is going$qb$, $qb$You should have kept the task yourself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone you delegated to has made a decision you would not have made. It is defensible. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Support the decision as it stands$qb$, $qb$Support it and discuss it with her later$qb$, $qb$Ask her to explain her reasoning first$qb$, $qb$Change it, since you are accountable for it$qb$, $qb$Let it stand but decide those yourself in future$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful sign that you have delegated something properly?$qb$, $qb$Decisions are being made without reaching you$qb$, $qb$The work is being completed on time$qb$, $qb$The person seems confident with the task$qb$, $qb$You are being kept informed of progress$qb$, $qb$The quality of the work is acceptable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are handing over a task permanently, not just once. What is most useful to hand over with it?$qb$, $qb$Whatever you use to judge whether it is going well$qb$, $qb$A written description of the steps involved$qb$, $qb$The contacts and access she will need$qb$, $qb$An explanation of why the task exists$qb$, $qb$A period of doing it together first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a sweet shop. Festival season starts in three weeks and you normally do all the ordering yourself. An experienced member of staff has offered to take it on. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Delegate ordering with clear spending and stock-out limits$qb$, $qb$Delegate ordering after reviewing last year's figures together$qb$, $qb$Delegate ordering but approve every order before it is placed$qb$, $qb$Delegate routine ordering but keep festival lines yourself$qb$, $qb$Keep all ordering because festival season is only three weeks away$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a tuition bus service. A driver has asked to take over the route planning, which you have always done. He knows the roads better than you. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Give him the routes and tell him what parents must not be asked to accept$qb$, $qb$Ask him to draft a plan and go through it with you before it runs$qb$, $qb$Give him one route to plan while you keep the rest for now$qb$, $qb$Let him plan them and check each one before it runs$qb$, $qb$Keep the planning, since parents complain to you about routes$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a silk reeling unit. You have given a supervisor responsibility for the reeling line, but the operators still come to you with every problem. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Send them back to him, and tell him what he can decide without asking you$qb$, $qb$Tell the operators to take problems to the supervisor$qb$, $qb$Ask the supervisor to be more visible on the line$qb$, $qb$Answer the questions and pass them on to him afterwards$qb$, $qb$Deal with the questions, since the operators are used to asking you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a bamboo furniture unit. You have handed a large order to a craftsman who is doing it his own way. His method is slower but the finish looks good. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Leave him to his method and judge it on the finished order$qb$, $qb$Ask him about the method and how long it will take$qb$, $qb$Ask him to use the faster method for the rest of the order$qb$, $qb$Watch the next few pieces before deciding anything$qb$, $qb$Take the order back onto the usual method$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a canal irrigation office. A junior clerk has been handling water release requests for a month and has made one decision you would have made differently. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask what she was weighing, then back her unless she was clearly wrong$qb$, $qb$Tell her how you would have decided it$qb$, $qb$Ask her to check with you on similar decisions$qb$, $qb$Review her recent decisions to see whether there is a pattern$qb$, $qb$Take those decisions back until she is more experienced$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supply printing ink. You have asked an assistant to handle small orders while you focus on large accounts. She keeps forwarding the small orders to you to approve. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Set the limit she can approve without you, and hold to it$qb$, $qb$Tell her she does not need to send small orders to you$qb$, $qb$Ask her why she is uncomfortable approving them$qb$, $qb$Approve them quickly so they are not delayed$qb$, $qb$Take the small orders back, since they are reaching you anyway$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an aquarium shop. You are away for a fortnight and a young assistant is covering. He has never handled a supplier dispute. How do you prepare him?$qb$, $qb$Agree what he can settle himself and when to hold something for your return$qb$, $qb$Tell him to call you if a dispute arises$qb$, $qb$Write down how to handle the disputes you can foresee$qb$, $qb$Ask a neighbouring shopkeeper to advise him if needed$qb$, $qb$Ask suppliers to hold any disputes until you are back$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a snack packaging line. You gave a team leader responsibility for shift changeovers. Changeovers are now slower than when you ran them. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask him what he is finding, and give it more time before judging$qb$, $qb$Ask him what is making the changeovers slower$qb$, $qb$Show him how you used to run the changeovers$qb$, $qb$Watch a changeover and see what is different$qb$, $qb$Take the changeovers back until output recovers$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a granite quarry office. You have delegated invoicing to a clerk. A customer has phoned you directly about an invoice query. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Pass the customer to the clerk and tell the customer why$qb$, $qb$Deal with the query and tell the clerk afterwards$qb$, $qb$Take the details and ask the clerk to call the customer back$qb$, $qb$Answer what you can and refer the rest to the clerk$qb$, $qb$Deal with it yourself, since the customer called you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a tourist camel camp. You have given a guide responsibility for the evening programme. He has changed it in a way guests seem to like but you find unprofessional. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask his objective, review guest impact, then set clear programme limits$qb$, $qb$Explain which parts of the changed programme seem unprofessional$qb$, $qb$Observe the changed programme again before giving any feedback$qb$, $qb$Ask several guests whether they prefer the changed programme$qb$, $qb$Tell him to restore the previous evening programme immediately$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a cotton ginning mill. You handed maintenance scheduling to a fitter. He has scheduled a shutdown in your busiest week. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell him what the busy week costs, and let him reschedule$qb$, $qb$Ask him why he chose that week$qb$, $qb$Tell him to move the shutdown to a quieter week$qb$, $qb$Move the shutdown yourself and tell him$qb$, $qb$Let it stand, since maintenance is now his to decide$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a wooden toy workshop. You gave a worker responsibility for a school order. She has come to you three times this week with questions she could answer. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what she thinks each time, and back her answer$qb$, $qb$Answer the questions and tell her she can decide these$qb$, $qb$Tell her which kinds of decision are hers to make$qb$, $qb$Answer them, since the school order matters$qb$, $qb$Take the order back, since she is not ready for it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You look after a sports ground. You have handed the pitch preparation to an assistant. A match is on Saturday and you are not confident the pitch will be ready. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask him what is left and agree what you will check on Friday$qb$, $qb$Ask him whether the pitch will be ready in time$qb$, $qb$Inspect the pitch yourself on Thursday$qb$, $qb$Work alongside him for the rest of the week$qb$, $qb$Take the preparation back for this match$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-DEL-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A5-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a papad making unit. You gave a worker responsibility for quality checks. She has been passing batches you would have rejected. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show her a batch you would reject and one you would pass$qb$, $qb$Tell her the standard is not being applied strictly enough$qb$, $qb$Ask her how she is deciding what to pass$qb$, $qb$Check the batches yourself for a week$qb$, $qb$Take the checks back, since the standard matters$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-001$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Giving the answer solves today's problem; asking the question builds the ability to solve ______.$qb$, $qb$tomorrow's$qb$, $qb$yours$qb$, $qb$several$qb$, $qb$theirs$qb$, $qb$routine work$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-003$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A learner who is never allowed to make a mistake never finds out where the ______ are.$qb$, $qb$limits$qb$, $qb$tools$qb$, $qb$rules$qb$, $qb$shortcuts$qb$, $qb$records$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-004$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Praising effort where the result was poor teaches the learner to trust neither the praise nor the ______.$qb$, $qb$criticism$qb$, $qb$task$qb$, $qb$trainer$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$result$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-005$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Showing someone once and watching them once teaches more than showing them ______.$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$slowly$qb$, $qb$carefully$qb$, $qb$again$qb$, $qb$together$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A person told what they did wrong still does not know what to do ______.$qb$, $qb$instead$qb$, $qb$practicaly$qb$, $qb$faster$qb$, $qb$again$qb$, $qb$first$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The best time to correct a habit is before it has been repeated ______.$qb$, $qb$often$qb$, $qb$publicly$qb$, $qb$badly$qb$, $qb$quickly$qb$, $qb$alone$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking a learner to explain it back reveals what the demonstration did not ______.$qb$, $qb$cover$qb$, $qb$cost$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$shorten$qb$, $qb$prove$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone learns faster when they know how their work will be ______.$qb$, $qb$judged$qb$, $qb$priced$qb$, $qb$utilized$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, $qb$copied$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A trainer who does the difficult part himself leaves the learner ready for only the ______ part.$qb$, $qb$easy$qb$, $qb$next$qb$, $qb$same$qb$, $qb$final$qb$, $qb$quick$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone corrected in front of others remembers being watched more clearly than what they were told to ______.$qb$, $qb$change$qb$, $qb$explain$qb$, $qb$repeat$qb$, $qb$perform$qb$, $qb$finish$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A learner who asks no questions may be lost rather than ______.$qb$, $qb$confident$qb$, $qb$present$qb$, $qb$creative$qb$, $qb$polite$qb$, $qb$arrogant$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The point of watching someone work is to see what they do when nobody ______.$qb$, $qb$helps$qb$, $qb$pays$qb$, $qb$asks$qb$, $qb$records$qb$, $qb$arrives$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Praise helps someone improve only when they can tell which part of their work earned it. Otherwise they have nothing to ______.$qb$, $qb$repeat$qb$, $qb$say$qb$, $qb$claim$qb$, $qb$share$qb$, $qb$finish$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A skill taught but never used again is forgotten before it is ______.$qb$, $qb$needed$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$judged$qb$, $qb$documented$qb$, $qb$discussed$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone you are training has asked you a question they could work out themselves. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they have already thought of$qb$, $qb$Answer it and explain how you worked it out$qb$, $qb$Point them to where the answer can be found$qb$, $qb$Answer it, since they have asked$qb$, $qb$Tell them to work it out themselves$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have shown someone a task and they have done it correctly once. What is best next?$qb$, $qb$Watch them do it without prompting$qb$, $qb$Show them the task a second time$qb$, $qb$Ask whether they have any questions$qb$, $qb$Let them get on with it alone$qb$, $qb$Ask them to explain it back to you$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A learner keeps making the same mistake after being corrected twice. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what they think they are doing at that step$qb$, $qb$Correct it a third time more clearly$qb$, $qb$Show them the step again slowly$qb$, $qb$Ask them to slow down at that point$qb$, $qb$Move them to work that does not involve it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful feedback to give someone who has done a task badly?$qb$, $qb$What to do differently next time$qb$, $qb$What went wrong with it$qb$, $qb$Where the standard was not met$qb$, $qb$How much it will cost to correct$qb$, $qb$That the work will need doing again$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are teaching something you find easy and they find hard. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out which step loses them$qb$, $qb$Break the task into smaller steps$qb$, $qb$Go through it more slowly$qb$, $qb$Explain it a different way$qb$, $qb$Give them more practice at it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone has improved but is still below the standard. What is best to say?$qb$, $qb$Name what improved and what is still missing$qb$, $qb$Tell them they are getting better$qb$, $qb$Tell them the standard is not yet met$qb$, $qb$Say nothing until the standard is met$qb$, $qb$Focus on the gap rather than the progress$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably tells you that someone has learned a task?$qb$, $qb$They handle a situation you did not cover$qb$, $qb$They complete it correctly on their own$qb$, $qb$They can explain how it is done$qb$, $qb$They no longer ask questions about it$qb$, $qb$They complete it as fast as you would$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A person you are developing has asked for feedback on work you have not seen. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Look at it, then ask what they think before giving your view$qb$, $qb$Look at it and give them your feedback$qb$, $qb$Ask what kind of feedback they want$qb$, $qb$Tell them you have not seen it and leave it there$qb$, $qb$Give a general view based on their usual work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have a learner who is confident but not yet competent. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Give them a task where the gap will show safely$qb$, $qb$Tell them where they still have gaps$qb$, $qb$Watch them more closely than the others$qb$, $qb$Slow down their progress until they catch up$qb$, $qb$Let experience correct the confidence$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when someone is corrected in front of the team?$qb$, $qb$They remember the setting more than the point$qb$, $qb$They become defensive about the work$qb$, $qb$They lose confidence in front of others$qb$, $qb$They stop asking questions in future$qb$, $qb$They correct the mistake but resent it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want someone to take on more difficult work. What is the most useful first step?$qb$, $qb$Give them a piece of it while you are around$qb$, $qb$Tell them you think they are ready$qb$, $qb$Ask whether they feel ready for it$qb$, $qb$Train them in the difficult parts first$qb$, $qb$Wait until they ask for more difficult work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A learner has done something in a way that works but that you would not use. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what led them to that way$qb$, $qb$Let it be, since it works$qb$, $qb$Show them the way you would use$qb$, $qb$Explain why your way is better$qb$, $qb$Ask them to use your way in future$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is most useful to establish before teaching someone a task?$qb$, $qb$What they already know about it$qb$, $qb$How quickly they need to learn it$qb$, $qb$How they prefer to be taught$qb$, $qb$Whether they want to learn it$qb$, $qb$How difficult the task is$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone has asked you to teach them something outside their current role. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find out what they want it for$qb$, $qb$Teach them, since they have asked$qb$, $qb$Check with their manager first$qb$, $qb$Explain that it is outside their role$qb$, $qb$Suggest they learn their current role better first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A person you trained has now trained someone else, and taught them a bad habit. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Go to the person you trained and work back from there$qb$, $qb$Correct the new person directly$qb$, $qb$Correct both of them together$qb$, $qb$Ask who else has been taught the same way$qb$, $qb$Retrain both from the beginning$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to do immediately after someone has struggled with a task?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they would do differently next time$qb$, $qb$Tell them what went wrong$qb$, $qb$Show them how it should be done$qb$, $qb$Reassure them that it takes practice$qb$, $qb$Let them try it again straight away$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are developing two people. One improves quickly, one slowly. What is most useful to ask?$qb$, $qb$Whether they are getting the same kind of work$qb$, $qb$What the slower one finds hardest about it$qb$, $qb$How each of them was taught the task$qb$, $qb$Whether the slower one is less motivated$qb$, $qb$Whether the faster one could take on more$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone you are coaching disagrees with your feedback. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they saw that you did not$qb$, $qb$Explain your reasoning more fully$qb$, $qb$Ask someone else to look at the work$qb$, $qb$Restate the feedback and move on$qb$, $qb$Accept their view and drop the point$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful question to ask a learner at the end of a task?$qb$, $qb$What surprised you$qb$, $qb$How did it go$qb$, $qb$What was hardest$qb$, $qb$Would you do it again$qb$, $qb$Did you finish on time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have limited time to develop someone. Where is that time best spent?$qb$, $qb$The thing that unlocks the most other work$qb$, $qb$The thing they are weakest at$qb$, $qb$The thing they most want to learn$qb$, $qb$The thing that is easiest to teach$qb$, $qb$The thing that will be needed soonest$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a bakery and have taken on an apprentice. Three weeks in, his shaping is improving but his timing is poor, so loaves go in late and come out uneven. He has not noticed the connection. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Have him watch two batches and work out why one came out better$qb$, $qb$Explain how the timing is affecting the loaves$qb$, $qb$Show him the timing you use and ask him to follow it$qb$, $qb$Take over the timing until his shaping is reliable$qb$, $qb$Wait, since his shaping is improving well$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a boat-building yard. A young worker has been fitting planks for a month. His work is sound but he checks with you before every single fitting. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Agree which fittings he can do without asking, and stick to it$qb$, $qb$Tell him his work is sound and he can proceed alone$qb$, $qb$Ask him what makes him unsure before each fitting$qb$, $qb$Answer the questions, since his work is coming out well$qb$, $qb$Tell him to stop checking and get on with it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You teach tabla. A student has good hand technique but poor timekeeping. He believes his problem is technique and practises that instead. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Record him playing and let him hear the timing for himself$qb$, $qb$Tell him his technique is fine and timing is the problem$qb$, $qb$Set him timing exercises alongside his technique practice$qb$, $qb$Play alongside him so he follows your timing$qb$, $qb$Let him practise technique, since he will notice eventually$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a dental laboratory. A technician's crowns are technically correct but take twice as long as anyone else's. She is thorough by nature. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Watch her work and find where the extra time actually goes$qb$, $qb$Tell her the crowns are taking too long$qb$, $qb$Ask her what takes her the most time$qb$, $qb$Set her a target time per crown$qb$, $qb$Leave her, since the crowns are technically correct$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a puncture repair shop by the roadside. A boy who helps you has learned to patch tubes but cannot yet judge which tubes are worth patching. How do you develop him?$qb$, $qb$Have him judge each tube first and say why, then check him$qb$, $qb$Show him what makes a tube not worth patching$qb$, $qb$Tell him to bring you any tube he is unsure about$qb$, $qb$Judge the tubes yourself and let him patch$qb$, $qb$Let him patch everything and learn from the failures$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a tea tasting room. A trainee taster gives descriptions that match yours because she hears you first. You cannot tell what she actually detects. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Have her taste and write her notes before you say anything$qb$, $qb$Ask her to describe the tea in her own words$qb$, $qb$Taste separately and compare notes afterwards$qb$, $qb$Tell her not to repeat what you have said$qb$, $qb$Continue, since her descriptions are accurate$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an animal shelter. A volunteer is gentle with the animals but avoids the difficult dogs. She has been volunteering for six months. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Work a difficult dog alongside her so the avoidance has support$qb$, $qb$Ask her what worries her about the difficult dogs$qb$, $qb$Tell her she needs to work with all the dogs$qb$, $qb$Pair her with an experienced volunteer for those dogs$qb$, $qb$Leave her with the animals she is comfortable with$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You lead a brass band. A new player is technically able but plays too loudly and unbalances the section. He cannot hear it from where he sits. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Move him to hear the section, then let him judge his own volume$qb$, $qb$Tell him he is playing too loudly for the section$qb$, $qb$Ask the section leader to speak to him about it$qb$, $qb$Record the band and play it back to him$qb$, $qb$Ask him to play more quietly in future$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You teach in a fishing village. A bright student stops trying whenever a topic looks hard, then says he is not good at it. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Give him a hard problem broken into steps he can each manage$qb$, $qb$Tell him he is capable and should keep trying$qb$, $qb$Ask him what makes him stop on the hard topics$qb$, $qb$Give him easier work so he builds confidence$qb$, $qb$Let him find his own level in each subject$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a carpet weaving unit. An experienced weaver has been asked to train a new one, but does the difficult knots herself to keep the pace up. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Agree how much slower the loom may run while the new weaver learns$qb$, $qb$Tell her the new weaver must do the difficult knots$qb$, $qb$Ask her why she is doing the knots herself$qb$, $qb$Move the training to a loom that is not on output$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the output is being maintained$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a ferry ticket office. A new clerk is accurate but freezes when a passenger becomes impatient. She has been in the role three weeks. How do you develop her?$qb$, $qb$Stand with her through two difficult passengers, then step back$qb$, $qb$Tell her what to say when a passenger becomes impatient$qb$, $qb$Ask her what happens for her in those moments$qb$, $qb$Take over whenever a passenger becomes impatient$qb$, $qb$Leave her, since three weeks is early for that$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a hand-block printing unit. A trainee's prints are clean but she always chooses the simplest block. The complex blocks are where the money is. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Give her a complex block with a spoiled cloth to practise on$qb$, $qb$Tell her she needs to move on to the complex blocks$qb$, $qb$Ask her what puts her off the complex blocks$qb$, $qb$Assign her complex blocks and check each print$qb$, $qb$Let her choose, since her prints are coming out clean$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a kirana store. A young assistant is good with regular customers but goes quiet with new ones. Trade depends on new customers staying. How do you develop him?$qb$, $qb$Agree one thing he will say to every new customer, and build from that$qb$, $qb$Tell him he needs to speak to new customers too$qb$, $qb$Ask him what is different about new customers$qb$, $qb$Handle the new customers yourself while he watches$qb$, $qb$Leave him with the regulars, since that works well$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-COD-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a honey bottling unit. A worker has learned every step but cannot tell when the filter needs changing. Getting it wrong spoils a batch. How do you develop her?$qb$, $qb$Have her judge the filter each day and compare with your call$qb$, $qb$Show her what a filter looks like when it needs changing$qb$, $qb$Tell her to ask you before every filter change$qb$, $qb$Change the filter yourself on a fixed schedule$qb$, $qb$Let her judge it and see how the batches come out$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-001$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$People work harder for a reason they understand than for a target they were simply ______.$qb$, $qb$given$qb$, $qb$shown$qb$, $qb$emailed$qb$, $qb$promised$qb$, $qb$expected$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-002$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A bonus paid months after the work was done feels less like recognition and more like ______.$qb$, $qb$wages$qb$, $qb$charity$qb$, $qb$penalty$qb$, $qb$interest$qb$, $qb$delay$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-003$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The quickest way to lower effort is to let poor work go ______.$qb$, $qb$unnoticed$qb$, $qb$unpaid$qb$, $qb$unfinished$qb$, $qb$unrecorded$qb$, $qb$unpriced$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-004$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who cannot see what their work leads to is being asked to trust the ______.$qb$, $qb$purpose$qb$, $qb$manager$qb$, $qb$wages$qb$, $qb$leadership$qb$, $qb$outcome$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-005$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Recognition given to the whole team when one person carried it teaches the rest that effort is ______.$qb$, $qb$optional$qb$, $qb$shared$qb$, $qb$costly$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$temporary$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-006$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A target nobody believes is reachable produces less effort than no target at ______.$qb$, $qb$all$qb$, $qb$first$qb$, $qb$once$qb$, $qb$work$qb$, $qb$home$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-007$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking people what would make the job better costs nothing until you ______ the answers.$qb$, $qb$ignore$qb$, $qb$praise$qb$, $qb$publish$qb$, $qb$approve$qb$, $qb$repeat$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-008$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Once someone considers their pay fair, extra effort is usually driven by something other than ______.$qb$, $qb$money$qb$, $qb$rules$qb$, $qb$targets$qb$, $qb$training$qb$, $qb$free hours$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-009$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A leader who only appears when something goes wrong becomes a sign of ______.$qb$, $qb$trouble$qb$, $qb$authority$qb$, $qb$progress$qb$, $qb$inspection$qb$, $qb$growth$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-010$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The strongest reason to do a job well is usually the person it ______.$qb$, $qb$affects$qb$, $qb$employs$qb$, $qb$pays$qb$, $qb$trains$qb$, $qb$allocates$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-011$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Praise given to everyone equally tells nobody what they did ______.$qb$, $qb$well$qb$, $qb$wrong$qb$, $qb$quickly$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$alone$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-012$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Effort falls fastest where people believe the outcome is already ______.$qb$, $qb$decided$qb$, $qb$recorded$qb$, $qb$published$qb$, $qb$lost$qb$, $qb$delayed$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Making the work visible to the people it helps does more than any ______.$qb$, $qb$speech$qb$, $qb$bonus$qb$, $qb$notice$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$target$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A promise of promotion that is not kept teaches people what your other promises are ______.$qb$, $qb$worth$qb$, $qb$for$qb$, $qb$about$qb$, $qb$hiding$qb$, $qb$recorded as$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Someone who is trusted with something difficult usually rises to ______.$qb$, $qb$it$qb$, $qb$them$qb$, $qb$notice$qb$, $qb$complain$qb$, $qb$ask$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team's output has dropped and nobody has complained. What is most useful to establish?$qb$, $qb$What has changed that nobody has mentioned$qb$, $qb$Whether the team is under more pressure$qb$, $qb$Whether the drop is real or a measurement issue$qb$, $qb$Which individuals have slowed down$qb$, $qb$Whether a target would bring output back up$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably makes people care about the standard of their work?$qb$, $qb$Seeing what happens to it after it leaves them$qb$, $qb$Knowing exactly what the standard is$qb$, $qb$Having their work checked against it regularly$qb$, $qb$Getting a reward for meeting it$qb$, $qb$Hearing why the standard was set$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member who used to volunteer for extra work has stopped. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what changed, without treating it as a problem$qb$, $qb$Ask whether something is wrong$qb$, $qb$Give the extra work to someone else$qb$, $qb$Ask him to take on the next piece$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since extra work is voluntary$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to lift a team that has become flat. What is most likely to work?$qb$, $qb$Remove one thing they find pointless$qb$, $qb$Set them a new and interesting target$qb$, $qb$Tell them what the work achieves$qb$, $qb$Bring in something to mark good work$qb$, $qb$Ask them what would make it better$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when one person's poor work is left uncorrected?$qb$, $qb$The people doing it well work less hard$qb$, $qb$The poor work becomes the accepted standard$qb$, $qb$The team loses respect for the manager$qb$, $qb$Others start covering for that person$qb$, $qb$Complaints reach the manager eventually$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A member of your team did something well three weeks ago. You have only just heard about it. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell them now, naming exactly what they did$qb$, $qb$Ask them to tell you how it went, then recognise it$qb$, $qb$Mention it at the next team meeting$qb$, $qb$Note it for their next review$qb$, $qb$Let it go, since three weeks is too late to matter$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team has been given a target they think is impossible. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what they think would be reachable$qb$, $qb$Explain why the target was set at that level$qb$, $qb$Break the target into smaller stages$qb$, $qb$Tell them to work towards it and see$qb$, $qb$Ask for the target to be reduced$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to know about someone before trying to motivate them?$qb$, $qb$What they would change about the job if they could$qb$, $qb$Where they want their career to go$qb$, $qb$Which parts of the work they find hardest$qb$, $qb$The tasks they are strongest at$qb$, $qb$How much they are paid$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A long project has months to run and the team has lost momentum. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Set something they can finish within a fortnight$qb$, $qb$Remind them what the project will achieve$qb$, $qb$Ask what is making it feel long$qb$, $qb$Bring the deadline forward to create urgency$qb$, $qb$Accept that long projects have flat periods$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been given a decision to pass on to your team that you disagree with. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Explain it accurately and say what you will do about your concerns$qb$, $qb$Explain the reasoning behind the decision$qb$, $qb$Pass it on and let them react$qb$, $qb$Tell them you disagree with it too$qb$, $qb$Pass it on as though you agree with it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two people do the same job. One is paid more for historical reasons and the other has found out. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$Whether the difference can be explained or must be fixed$qb$, $qb$How the second person found out$qb$, $qb$Whether the difference is large$qb$, $qb$Whether others know about it$qb$, $qb$Whether the pay can be adjusted$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is most likely to make someone stop putting in extra effort?$qb$, $qb$Seeing that it made no difference$qb$, $qb$Not being thanked for it$qb$, $qb$Being asked for more$qb$, $qb$Seeing others do less$qb$, $qb$Being tired$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A quiet team member does good work but never puts himself forward. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Give him something visible that he will do well$qb$, $qb$Tell him his work is valued$qb$, $qb$Ask whether he wants more responsibility$qb$, $qb$Mention his work to your own manager$qb$, $qb$Leave him, since he seems content$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are taking over a team that has been badly managed. What is most useful in the first month?$qb$, $qb$Fix one thing they have complained about for years$qb$, $qb$Tell them how things will be different$qb$, $qb$Meet each of them individually$qb$, $qb$Set clear expectations from the start$qb$, $qb$Wait and see how the team works$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually gives a job meaning for the person doing it?$qb$, $qb$Knowing who is worse off if it is done badly$qb$, $qb$Understanding how it fits the wider work$qb$, $qb$Being told the work is important$qb$, $qb$Being paid fairly for it$qb$, $qb$Having some choice in how it is done$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team achieved something difficult. What is the most useful response?$qb$, $qb$Say what each person did that made it work$qb$, $qb$Thank the team for the achievement$qb$, $qb$Mark it with something the team will enjoy$qb$, $qb$Report the achievement to senior management$qb$, $qb$Move straight on to the next piece of work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone has told you they are thinking of leaving. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what would have kept them, whether or not they stay$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make them stay$qb$, $qb$Ask why they are thinking of leaving$qb$, $qb$Offer what you are able to offer$qb$, $qb$Accept it and plan for their replacement$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team works well but is given work nobody thinks matters. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find out who the work actually serves and tell them$qb$, $qb$Tell the team the work matters$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the work is still needed$qb$, $qb$Make the work as quick to do as possible$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the work is being done$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to do when a team has failed at something?$qb$, $qb$Name what they got right before what went wrong$qb$, $qb$Establish what went wrong$qb$, $qb$Move quickly on to the next attempt$qb$, $qb$Take the blame yourself$qb$, $qb$Let them recover before discussing it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have almost nothing to offer by way of reward or promotion. What is left?$qb$, $qb$Control over how the work is done$qb$, $qb$Praise for work done well$qb$, $qb$Clear explanations of decisions$qb$, $qb$Fair allocation of the unpopular tasks$qb$, $qb$Nothing much, without something to offer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run the night shift at a bottling plant. Output on nights has been below days for six months. The night team say days get the newer machines. Your checks show the machines are similar. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show them the machine figures and ask what else is different at night$qb$, $qb$Tell them the machines are similar and the gap is not the machines$qb$, $qb$Ask the day shift what they do differently$qb$, $qb$Set the night team the same target as days$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since night output is always lower$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a chain of street-food carts. One cart's staff are cheerful and one cart's are flat, though pay and hours are identical. Takings match the mood. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Spend a shift at the flat cart and find what is different there$qb$, $qb$Ask the flat cart's staff what would improve the job$qb$, $qb$Move a cheerful worker to the flat cart$qb$, $qb$Set the flat cart a takings target to work towards$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the takings difference is small$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a rural post office with three staff. A new counter system has doubled their keystrokes and they now finish each day tired and irritable. You cannot change the system. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find what else you can take off them to offset the extra work$qb$, $qb$Ask head office to review the system$qb$, $qb$Tell them the system cannot be changed$qb$, $qb$Praise them for coping with the extra work$qb$, $qb$Wait, since they will get faster with practice$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a dance school. A talented student has stopped putting effort into class since she was not chosen for the lead. She still attends. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Give her something she can own in the next performance$qb$, $qb$Explain why she was not chosen for the lead$qb$, $qb$Tell her that effort now affects future casting$qb$, $qb$Ask her whether she still wants to be here$qb$, $qb$Leave her, since she is still attending$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a tyre retreading works. A worker has suggested improvements four times and none has been acted on. He has stopped suggesting anything. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Take one of his four suggestions and act on it now$qb$, $qb$Explain why the four suggestions were not taken up$qb$, $qb$Ask him to keep making suggestions$qb$, $qb$Tell him his suggestions were appreciated$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since suggestions are voluntary$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a community kitchen with volunteers. Numbers have dropped from twenty to eight over a year. Nobody has said why they stopped coming. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Contact some of the twelve and ask what changed for them$qb$, $qb$Ask the eight who remain why others might have left$qb$, $qb$Recruit new volunteers to replace the twelve$qb$, $qb$Make the sessions shorter to be less demanding$qb$, $qb$Carry on with eight, since the work is getting done$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a waste segregation crew. The work is unpleasant and the crew take longer breaks than agreed. Output still meets the minimum. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what would make the shift bearable, then trade that against the breaks$qb$, $qb$Tell them the breaks must return to the agreed length$qb$, $qb$Ask them why the breaks have got longer$qb$, $qb$Set a higher output target so breaks have to shorten$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since output still meets the minimum$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a fish drying yard. Workers are paid by the tray and one group has started rushing, producing trays that dry unevenly. Quality is not measured. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Start measuring quality and pay against it$qb$, $qb$Tell them the trays are drying unevenly$qb$, $qb$Ask them why they have started rushing$qb$, $qb$Slow the pace by reducing the trays available$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since they are paid by the tray$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a night watchman team of six across three sites. They rarely see you or each other and several have become careless about logging rounds. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Visit each site at night and go round with them once$qb$, $qb$Remind them that logging rounds is required$qb$, $qb$Ask them why the logs have become patchy$qb$, $qb$Introduce a check that the logs are completed$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since nothing has gone wrong$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a quarry canteen. Your two cooks work hard but say nobody notices what they do. The quarry workers eat quickly and leave. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Arrange for the cooks to hear directly from the workers who eat there$qb$, $qb$Tell the cooks that their work is appreciated$qb$, $qb$Ask the quarry manager to thank them$qb$, $qb$Put up a notice naming the cooks$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the meals are being produced$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a hand-loom dyeing shed. Your most skilled dyer has become slow and withdrawn since a younger worker was promoted over him. His quality is unchanged. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask what he wants from the next two years here$qb$, $qb$Explain why the younger worker was promoted$qb$, $qb$Tell him his skill is still valued$qb$, $qb$Give him more responsibility to compensate$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since his quality has not dropped$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a matchbox packing unit employing twenty women. Attendance drops sharply in the two weeks before harvest each year. It happens every year. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Plan the year around it and agree the arrangement with them$qb$, $qb$Ask them why attendance falls at that time$qb$, $qb$Offer a bonus for attendance in those weeks$qb$, $qb$Hire temporary workers for the two weeks$qb$, $qb$Accept the drop, since it happens every year$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a cinema projection room with two operators. The job is now largely automatic and both have become bored and inattentive. Faults have gone unnoticed twice. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Give them something in the cinema that uses their attention$qb$, $qb$Tell them the faults must be caught$qb$, $qb$Introduce a check they must complete each screening$qb$, $qb$Ask them whether the job has become boring$qb$, $qb$Reduce the room to one operator$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-MOT-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A5-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a bus depot cleaning crew of eight. They finish faster than the time allowed and spend the remainder sitting. The buses are clean. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Discuss useful extra responsibilities and what recognition they expect$qb$, $qb$Assign additional duties so the crew remains busy for the full shift$qb$, $qb$Reduce the cleaning time allowance to match their current pace$qb$, $qb$Ask the crew why they consistently finish the cleaning so early$qb$, $qb$Leave the arrangement unchanged because the buses are clean$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
