  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-FIB-013$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Long-term aims survive short-term pressure only when someone keeps ______ them.$qb$, $qb$naming$qb$, $qb$funding$qb$, $qb$measuring$qb$, $qb$recording$qb$, $qb$announcing$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A goal that cannot be turned into this month's work is not yet a ______.$qb$, $qb$plan$qb$, $qb$priority$qb$, $qb$forecast$qb$, $qb$budget$qb$, $qb$commitment$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$When each department is judged only on its own figures, the business can pull in several ______.$qb$, $qb$directions$qb$, $qb$budgets$qb$, $qb$timetables$qb$, $qb$markets$qb$, $qb$standards$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Asking people what the aim means for their own work turns listening into ______.$qb$, $qb$alignment$qb$, $qb$agreement$qb$, $qb$consultation$qb$, $qb$instruction$qb$, $qb$negotiation$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-FIB-017$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A reason given once at a meeting reaches only the people who were ______.$qb$, $qb$there$qb$, $qb$invited$qb$, $qb$senior$qb$, $qb$responsible$qb$, $qb$expected$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team can recite the company's stated aim but their daily work has not changed. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Work out with them what the aim rules out this month$qb$, $qb$Explain the aim again in plainer words$qb$, $qb$Set targets that follow from the aim$qb$, $qb$Ask them what they think the aim means$qb$, $qb$Wait, since changes of this kind take time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A long-term goal has been set for three years out. What makes it more than a statement?$qb$, $qb$Something in this quarter is different because of it$qb$, $qb$It has been written down and circulated$qb$, $qb$Everyone can explain what it means$qb$, $qb$It has a budget attached$qb$, $qb$Progress against it is reported$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two departments are each meeting their targets and undercutting one another. What is most useful to establish?$qb$, $qb$What each department believes it is there to achieve$qb$, $qb$Whose targets should change$qb$, $qb$Which department is causing the greater damage$qb$, $qb$Whether the two sets of targets conflict$qb$, $qb$How long the situation has been going on$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are explaining a new direction to people who will have to change how they work. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$What each of them will stop doing$qb$, $qb$Why the direction was chosen$qb$, $qb$What the direction is$qb$, $qb$When the change takes effect$qb$, $qb$Who decided on it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team accepts the direction in principle but says it cannot be reached from where they stand today. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Map what would have to be true at each stage between here and there$qb$, $qb$Explain why the direction was chosen$qb$, $qb$Set a first stage they can see a path through$qb$, $qb$Ask them to begin and review in six months$qb$, $qb$Take their view upward and ask for the direction to change$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most often causes a stated priority to be ignored?$qb$, $qb$Nothing was taken off the list when it was added$qb$, $qb$The explanation was not clear enough$qb$, $qb$People privately disagreed with it$qb$, $qb$No measure was attached to it$qb$, $qb$The priority kept changing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have inherited a team with no shared sense of where the work is going. What is the most useful first step?$qb$, $qb$Ask each of them what they think the team is for$qb$, $qb$Tell them what the team is for$qb$, $qb$Set a shared goal for the coming quarter$qb$, $qb$Review what the team has been working on$qb$, $qb$Wait until you understand the work better$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A member of your team keeps working on something outside the agreed direction, and doing it well. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Show him where the direction leaves his work, and decide together$qb$, $qb$Ask him why he is working on it$qb$, $qb$Tell him to move onto the agreed work$qb$, $qb$Let it continue, since the work is good$qb$, $qb$Report it to whoever set the direction$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main weakness of a vision expressed only in general words?$qb$, $qb$Nobody can tell what it rules out$qb$, $qb$It is hard to remember$qb$, $qb$It sounds like every other company's$qb$, $qb$It cannot be measured$qb$, $qb$People do not believe it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team has been given a new direction and one part of it contradicts what you told them three months ago. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say plainly what has changed and what you got wrong$qb$, $qb$Explain the new direction and the reasoning behind it$qb$, $qb$Present the new direction without referring to the old one$qb$, $qb$Say the earlier position was never firm$qb$, $qb$Let the team notice the difference themselves$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A five-year aim has been set and nothing has been dropped from the current workload. What follows?$qb$, $qb$The aim will lose to whatever is urgent$qb$, $qb$The team will be overloaded$qb$, $qb$The aim will take longer than planned$qb$, $qb$Some work will be done badly$qb$, $qb$The aim will need extra people$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A difficult quarter has pushed the long-term aim out of every conversation. What holds it in place?$qb$, $qb$Someone connects this quarter's decisions back to it out loud$qb$, $qb$The aim is reported on each month$qb$, $qb$The aim has a budget protected for it$qb$, $qb$Senior people repeat the aim regularly$qb$, $qb$The aim is written into people's objectives$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are choosing between two projects. One fits the stated direction, one earns more this year. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Say plainly what taking the earner costs the direction$qb$, $qb$Work out how much more the earner brings in$qb$, $qb$Ask whoever set the direction to decide$qb$, $qb$Take the earner, since this year is certain$qb$, $qb$Take the one that fits, since the direction is agreed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Someone transferring in from another department asks what your team is trying to achieve. What is most useful to tell them?$qb$, $qb$Which of their new tasks feeds the aim, and which does not$qb$, $qb$What the long-term aim is$qb$, $qb$How the direction came to be set$qb$, $qb$What the team has in hand this month$qb$, $qb$Who decided the direction$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team's work supports an aim they never see the results of. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Show them where their part ends up$qb$, $qb$Explain the aim to them again$qb$, $qb$Report progress against the aim regularly$qb$, $qb$Ask them whether they understand the aim$qb$, $qb$Set them targets tied to the aim$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when every piece of work is described as a priority?$qb$, $qb$The choice of what to drop passes to whoever is busiest$qb$, $qb$Nothing is treated as a priority$qb$, $qb$People work longer hours$qb$, $qb$Quality falls across the work$qb$, $qb$Deadlines start to slip$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to turn a broad aim into work for the next three months. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$Naming what will be visibly different at the end of the three months$qb$, $qb$Listing the tasks that follow from the aim$qb$, $qb$Agreeing who is responsible for each part$qb$, $qb$Setting a measure for progress$qb$, $qb$Checking the aim is understood first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague says the direction is just words from senior management. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask which part of his work it does not fit$qb$, $qb$Explain why the direction matters$qb$, $qb$Agree that it is broadly worded$qb$, $qb$Tell him to raise it with senior management$qb$, $qb$Ignore it, since he may not be persuadable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You want to know whether your team is genuinely pulling the same way. What would show it?$qb$, $qb$They turn down work that does not fit$qb$, $qb$They can all describe the aim$qb$, $qb$They meet their targets$qb$, $qb$They work well together$qb$, $qb$They agree with the direction$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a language school. You have told staff the aim is to become the school people choose for exam preparation. Teachers still fill their timetables with general classes because those are easier to fill. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Agree with them which general classes stop, so exam classes have room$qb$, $qb$Explain again why exam preparation is the aim$qb$, $qb$Set each teacher a target for exam classes$qb$, $qb$Ask them why they prefer general classes$qb$, $qb$Wait, since exam demand will grow on its own$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a car parts distributor. The stated aim is same-week delivery to workshops. Your warehouse team is measured on picking accuracy alone and delivery has not improved. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change what the warehouse is measured on so it carries the aim$qb$, $qb$Explain to the warehouse team why delivery matters$qb$, $qb$Add a delivery target alongside the accuracy one$qb$, $qb$Ask the warehouse team what slows delivery$qb$, $qb$Raise the delivery problem with whoever set the measures$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a bottled water plant. You have set a three-year aim to supply hotels rather than shops. Nothing in this year's plan is different. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Decide now what comes out of this year's plan to make room$qb$, $qb$Add hotel work to this year's plan$qb$, $qb$Explain the three-year aim to the management team$qb$, $qb$Set a target for hotel customers this year$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since three years allows time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a shoe factory. Two supervisors are each meeting their output targets, but one is producing sizes the other cannot pair. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Agree with both what a finished pair means, then set the targets to that$qb$, $qb$Change the targets so they match each other$qb$, $qb$Ask the two supervisors to coordinate between themselves$qb$, $qb$Find out which supervisor's sizes are wrong$qb$, $qb$Raise it with whoever sets the targets$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a packaging plant. Your stated aim is to move into food-grade work, which needs cleaner lines. Operators say nothing has changed for them. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Name one thing on each line that changes this month$qb$, $qb$Explain what food-grade work will require$qb$, $qb$Bring forward the cleaning standards now$qb$, $qb$Ask operators what would have to change$qb$, $qb$Wait until the food-grade orders arrive$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a bus company. You have said the aim is to become the reliable operator on your routes. Drivers are still paid a bonus for passenger numbers. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change the bonus so it pays for the thing you have asked for$qb$, $qb$Explain to drivers why reliability matters more$qb$, $qb$Add a punctuality element to the bonus$qb$, $qb$Ask drivers what stops them running to time$qb$, $qb$Leave the bonus and monitor punctuality separately$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a fruit packhouse. Your long-term aim is export work. A large domestic order has come in that would fill the season and use all your capacity. How do you decide?$qb$, $qb$Set out what the season costs the export aim, then decide openly$qb$, $qb$Work out what the domestic order earns against export prices$qb$, $qb$Ask the export customers whether they can wait$qb$, $qb$Take the order, since it fills the season$qb$, $qb$Refuse it, since the aim is export work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a metal fabrication shop. You have told the team the aim is to take on more complex work. Nobody is being trained and the simple jobs still fill the week. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Free one day a week for complex work and put someone on it$qb$, $qb$Arrange training for the complex work$qb$, $qb$Explain the aim to the team again$qb$, $qb$Turn down some simple jobs to make room$qb$, $qb$Wait until a complex job comes in$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a soap factory. Your aim is to reduce reliance on one large buyer. Your sales team is paid on total volume, and the large buyer is the easiest volume. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change how sales are paid so new buyers are worth finding$qb$, $qb$Set the sales team a target for new buyers$qb$, $qb$Explain the risk of relying on one buyer$qb$, $qb$Ask the sales team why they favour the large buyer$qb$, $qb$Approach new buyers yourself$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a paint factory. Senior management has announced a new direction you were not consulted on and partly disagree with. Your team is asking what it means. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set out the direction accurately and say what you will raise upward$qb$, $qb$Explain the direction and the reasoning behind it$qb$, $qb$Tell them the direction and let them form a view$qb$, $qb$Tell them you disagree with parts of it$qb$, $qb$Present it as though you agree with all of it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a garment factory. Your stated aim is to shorten lead times. A supervisor has found a way to do this on his line but it lowers his output figure. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Change the figure he is judged on, and show the others what he did$qb$, $qb$Tell him his output figure will be overlooked this month$qb$, $qb$Record the method so it survives beyond his line$qb$, $qb$Tell him to keep the method and accept the lower figure$qb$, $qb$Ask him to return to the method that protects his output$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a bicycle factory. Your team knows the aim is to build for city riders rather than sport. Designers still bring you sport-oriented ideas. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Work through one idea with them to show where the aim leads it$qb$, $qb$Remind them that the aim is city riders$qb$, $qb$Reject sport ideas as they arrive$qb$, $qb$Ask them why they keep returning to sport$qb$, $qb$Accept the ideas, since good ideas are scarce$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-VSA-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A5-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a window manufacturer. You set a four-year aim in January. The team has been under heavy pressure since March and the aim has not been mentioned in any meeting since then. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Point out in this quarter's decisions where the aim is being traded away$qb$, $qb$Bring the aim back onto the agenda next quarter$qb$, $qb$Remind the team of the aim at the next meeting$qb$, $qb$Protect one small piece of work tied to the aim$qb$, $qb$Leave it until the pressure eases$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
