  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a bus workshop. A fitter tells you he fitted a part wrongly last week and the bus has been in service since. Two others are in the room. You will have the bus checked either way. How do you respond to him?$qb$, $qb$Say in front of the others that he was right to come forward$qb$, $qb$Work out with him how the wrong part came to be fitted$qb$, $qb$Thank him privately once the others have gone$qb$, $qb$Record the error against him$qb$, $qb$Tell him to be more careful in future$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a car hire depot. A new member of staff has twice started to say something in the morning briefing and stopped. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask her directly for her view on the next point$qb$, $qb$Ask her afterwards what she was going to say$qb$, $qb$Invite anyone who has not spoken to contribute$qb$, $qb$Wait until she is more settled$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since she can speak if she wishes$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a paper bag factory. A machine operator says the new glue is failing. Your supervisor said the same last month and you dismissed it. You are going to test the glue. What else do you do?$qb$, $qb$Tell them both you were wrong to dismiss it last month$qb$, $qb$Ask each of them what they have been seeing$qb$, $qb$Report the test result to the floor when it comes$qb$, $qb$Check with the glue supplier before saying anything$qb$, $qb$Say nothing about last month$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a candle factory. In your production meetings the same three people speak and the other seven never do. This has been true for a year. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find out what happened the last time one of the seven spoke$qb$, $qb$Ask each of the seven directly for their view$qb$, $qb$Ask the three to leave space for others$qb$, $qb$Ask the seven privately whether they have concerns$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the three raise what matters$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a brush factory. A worker reported a safety concern that turned out to be mistaken. The floor knows she raised it. What do you do now?$qb$, $qb$Tell the floor what you checked and that she was right to raise it$qb$, $qb$Ask her to walk you through what she saw$qb$, $qb$Explain to her privately why the concern was unfounded$qb$, $qb$Announce that the concern was checked and was fine$qb$, $qb$Say nothing further, since there was no problem$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a ceramic sanitaryware factory. A kiln loader disagreed with you in front of the shift and was right. The shift is watching. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say plainly that he was right and change the loading$qb$, $qb$Ask him to set out the change to the shift himself$qb$, $qb$Change the loading and thank him afterwards$qb$, $qb$Say the point will be looked at and move on$qb$, $qb$Change it later so it does not look like a reversal$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
