  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage valve manufacturing. An operator has been quietly correcting a design error for months rather than reporting it. You have just found out. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Find out what made reporting it feel worse than fixing it$qb$, $qb$Thank him for the corrections and fix the design$qb$, $qb$Ask him why he did not report it$qb$, $qb$Fix the design and remind the team to report errors$qb$, $qb$Tell him errors must be reported in future$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a gearbox repair shop. A trainee has damaged an expensive part and told you at once. The shop is small and everyone will hear. The part will be replaced either way. How do you handle him?$qb$, $qb$Let the shop hear that telling you early was the right move$qb$, $qb$Work out with him how the damage happened$qb$, $qb$Speak to him privately about it$qb$, $qb$Record the cost of the part against the job$qb$, $qb$Warn him what the part has cost$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
