  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a juice bottling plant. A line worker has raised the same concern three times and nothing has been done about it. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell her what happened after each of the three times she raised it, address the concern now, and explain how it will be followed up.$qb$, $qb$Review the concern promptly and tell her when she will receive a decision.$qb$, $qb$Explain why it has not been acted on$qb$, $qb$Ask her to raise it again through her supervisor$qb$, $qb$Apologise and add it to the list$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-PSC-SJT-049$qb$, $qb$A5-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an animal feed mill. Your shift leader admits he took a shortcut that could have affected a batch. He told you before anyone noticed. The batch will be checked. What matters most in how you treat the admission?$qb$, $qb$The mill sees early admission treated as the right move$qb$, $qb$You find out what pushed him into the shortcut$qb$, $qb$He is spoken to privately about it$qb$, $qb$The incident goes onto the record$qb$, $qb$He is warned about shortcuts$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
