  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A word means one thing in your team and another in theirs. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Describe what you mean rather than name it$qb$, $qb$Agree a shared definition$qb$, $qb$Use their word when talking to them$qb$, $qb$Explain how your team uses the word$qb$, $qb$Avoid the word altogether$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens to a problem that falls between two departments?$qb$, $qb$It grows until it becomes someone's emergency$qb$, $qb$Each assumes the other is dealing with it$qb$, $qb$It is escalated to a common manager$qb$, $qb$Nobody has the authority to fix it$qb$, $qb$It is discussed but not resolved$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
