  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two teams have agreed a way of working and it has already broken down. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out which team's daily pressures it did not survive$qb$, $qb$Remind both teams what was agreed$qb$, $qb$Ask both managers to reinforce it$qb$, $qb$Find out who stopped following it$qb$, $qb$Agree a simpler way of working$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your department's output becomes another department's input. What most reduces friction at that join?$qb$, $qb$Each side knowing what the other does with it$qb$, $qb$A written specification for the handover$qb$, $qb$Regular meetings between the two$qb$, $qb$A single named contact on each side$qb$, $qb$Agreed deadlines for the handover$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A department you rely on has a new manager who does things differently. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what he has been brought in to change$qb$, $qb$Explain how the two departments have worked until now$qb$, $qb$Ask him how he would like requests to reach him$qb$, $qb$Carry on as before and see what happens$qb$, $qb$Wait until he has settled in before approaching him$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A decision by another department has made your work harder. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find out what the decision was solving for them$qb$, $qb$Tell them what it has done to your work$qb$, $qb$Ask them to reverse it$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your own manager$qb$, $qb$Work around it and say nothing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What tells you two departments have genuinely started working together?$qb$, $qb$They raise each other's problems before being asked$qb$, $qb$They share information readily$qb$, $qb$They meet regularly$qb$, $qb$Their managers speak often$qb$, $qb$Complaints between them have stopped$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your department and another are both cutting cost, and the cheapest option for you costs them more. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Put both figures together before either of you decides$qb$, $qb$Look for an option that saves both$qb$, $qb$Ask them what their cheapest option would be$qb$, $qb$Take your saving and let them raise it$qb$, $qb$Take the saving, since each department is judged separately$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main weakness of solving a cross-department problem through managers only?$qb$, $qb$The people doing the work never agree anything$qb$, $qb$The detail gets lost between them$qb$, $qb$The teams learn nothing about each other$qb$, $qb$It becomes a matter of authority$qb$, $qb$It takes longer than it needs to$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Something your department did last week has caused another department a problem they have not yet traced to you. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Go to them now and say what it means for their work$qb$, $qb$Fix it at your end before they find out$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager and let him inform them$qb$, $qb$Wait to see whether they trace it$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since they have not noticed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage production at a factory. Quality keeps rejecting batches you consider acceptable and output is suffering. Quality say they are only applying the standard. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out what quality are judged on before arguing about the batches$qb$, $qb$Go through the rejected batches with quality together$qb$, $qb$Ask quality to explain the standard they are applying$qb$, $qb$Escalate the rejection rate to your director$qb$, $qb$Produce to the tighter standard and accept the slower output$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a hotel kitchen. Reception keeps promising guests meal times the kitchen cannot meet, and guests complain to the kitchen. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out what reception are trying to avoid when they promise$qb$, $qb$Tell reception what times the kitchen can actually meet$qb$, $qb$Ask reception to check with the kitchen before promising$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the hotel manager$qb$, $qb$Meet the promised times and accept the pressure$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in college admissions. Finance holds up offers while fees are checked and applicants go elsewhere. Finance say the checks are required. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Find out what finance are protecting against, then look for a faster route$qb$, $qb$Show finance how many applicants are lost to the delay$qb$, $qb$Ask finance to prioritise the offer checks$qb$, $qb$Send offers before finance have checked$qb$, $qb$Raise the delay with the principal$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-CFS-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A5-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are an estimator for a builder. Site staff say your estimates never match the real job, and you say they never work to the estimate. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Walk one job through with the site team from estimate to finish$qb$, $qb$Compare your estimates against actual costs on recent jobs$qb$, $qb$Ask the site team where the estimates go wrong$qb$, $qb$Build more contingency into future estimates$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager to settle the difference$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
